<section id="cot-conclusion" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Use the Cotangent Ratio With Confidence</h2>
  <p>Cotangent is the flipped form of tangent: divide the adjacent side by the opposite side and you have described the triangle's run-to-rise shape. The formula <span set:html={rich('[[\\cot(A)=b/a]]')} /> needs only two measurements, the answer is always a positive dimensionless number, and it can sit above, at, or below 1 depending on which leg is longer. When the angle itself is needed, <span set:html={rich('[[A=\\tan^{-1}(a/b)]]')} /> recovers it. Ladder, roof, ramp, or textbook 3-4-5, the method never changes: identify the adjacent side, identify the opposite side, divide, and verify with the reciprocal of tangent.</p>
</section>
